      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <climits>\n#include <cassert>\n\nint main() {\n\tint n,s;\n\tstd::cin >> n >> s;\n\n\t// Read matrix and compute column prefix sums in one pass.\n\t// pref[i*n + j] = sum of rows 0..i-1 at column j, for i=0..n.\n\tstd::vector<int> pref((n+1) * n, 0);\n\tfor (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n\t\tfor (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n\t\t\tint val;\n\t\t\tscanf(\"%d\", &val);\n\t\t\tpref[i*n + j] = pref[(i-1)*n + j] + val;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tassert(s < n && s > 0 && n > 0 && n < 8000);\n\n\tint mxSum = INT_MIN;\n\n\t// Each starting row is independent; use OpenMP reduction over rows.\n\t#pragma omp parallel for reduction(max:mxSum) schedule(dynamic,64)\n\tfor (int i = 0; i <= n - s; ++i) {\n\t\tconst int rowStart = i * n;\n\t\tconst int rowEnd   = (i + s) * n;\n\n\t\t// Initial horizontal window for columns 0..s-1.\n\t\tint window = 0;\n\t\tfor (int j = 0; j < s; ++j) {\n\t\t\twindow += pref[rowEnd + j] - pref[rowStart + j];\n\t\t}\n\t\tint curMax = window;\n\n\t\t// Slide the window to the right.\n\t\tfor (int j = s; j < n; ++j) {\n\t\t\twindow += (pref[rowEnd + j] - pref[rowStart + j])\n\t\t\t        - (pref[rowEnd + (j-s)] - pref[rowStart + (j-s)]);\n\t\t\tif (window > curMax) curMax = window;\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tif (curMax > mxSum) mxSum = curMax;\n\t}\n\n\tprintf(\"%d\\n\", mxSum);\n\treturn 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Using dynamic scheduling with a moderate chunk size improves load balance for the row-parallel reduction loop on 4 cores by allowing work stealing when iteration counts are not perfectly divisible or cache effects cause variable per-row times, while keeping overhead low compared to guided/static variants.",
  "notes": "Fixed missing <cassert> include that caused compilation failure. Changed OpenMP schedule from static to dynamic with chunk size 64 to test whether adaptive scheduling reduces tail imbalance for the uniform row loop without excessive runtime overhead on 4 cores.",
